<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="045" project="spaarkeai-compose-r8">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-A10 — Publish the residual loss list with owner sign-off, and merge the ADR-049 third amendment (7 invariants) — MAIN SESSION ONLY</title>
    <phase>4 Track A — Faithful Save</phase>
    <gate>blocked-on-031</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Writes a binding ADR amendment and the published contract for what Compose does not preserve. PROVISIONAL — amendable by task 031.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Capability-matched: the amendment's wording binds future releases, and the residual list is the document a user is entitled to rely on. Both fail silently when subtly wrong — an invariant stated loosely gets traded away in R9, and a residual list that does not match the gate means we are losing something we told nobody about.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Writes `.claude/adr/` — main session only (root §3). Depends on all Track A outcomes.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>040, 041, 042, 043, 044</deps>
    <tags>architecture, documentation, compose</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    ⚠️ **MAIN SESSION ONLY.** This task writes to `.claude/adr/`. Sub-agents launched via the Agent tool
    CANNOT write these paths (root CLAUDE.md §3) — that boundary is intentional. The main session applies
    these edits directly.

    Two deliverables that close Track A:

    **FR-A10 — The residual loss list.** Publish, in `docs/architecture/`, exactly what Compose does NOT
    preserve, and get owner sign-off. The list MUST match what the gate enforces: no construct may degrade
    that is not on the list, and nothing on the list may be something the gate actually preserves. That parity
    is the whole value — a residual list that drifts from the gate is a promise nobody is keeping.

    **The ADR-049 third amendment.** Task 031 drafted it in `projects/.../notes/`. Apply it to
    `.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md`, carrying the seven standing invariants and, critically,
    the rule that invariants (1) "every save terminates in a defined outcome" and (2) "untouched blocks are
    preserved" are a PAIR no future amendment may trade away singly. Both prior amendments traded one for the
    other; that is the pendulum this wording stops.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE architect. Authority to amend ADRs and publish architecture documentation. Familiar with ADR-049's full history and root CLAUDE.md §6.5.</role>

  <goal>
    ADR-049 carries the third amendment with all seven invariants and the paired-MUST rule. A residual loss
    list is published in `docs/architecture/`, owner-signed-off, and in demonstrated parity with the gate.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Success criterion 5 of the spec is "zero silent loss; residual list published and matching the gate".
      "Matching" is the operative word — the parity check is what converts a document into a guarantee.

      The seven invariants are already stated in the project CLAUDE.md and drafted in task 031. This task's
      job is to move them into the binding location with wording that survives the next project's pressure.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="primary-edit">.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file role="doc-output">docs/architecture/ (residual loss list — write-side companion)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/adr-049-third-amendment-draft.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/gate-decision.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/Compose/ComposeFidelityGateHarnessTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §3">MAIN SESSION ONLY for the `.claude/adr/` write. Sub-agents cannot write these paths; if an "Edit denied" appears, that is the boundary working, not a bug.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The amendment MUST declare invariants (1) and (2) as a PAIR no future amendment may trade away singly. This exact wording is the structural guard — do not soften it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The amendment MUST state invariant (7) — "deterministic information available at capture time MUST be carried, not re-derived" — as a GENERAL rule, not per-surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The residual list MUST be in demonstrated parity with the gate: for every construct family, either the gate preserves it OR it is on the list. Demonstrate the parity, do not assert it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §6.5">This is a Path-B amendment. It MUST merge with or before the dependent code — it cannot trail Track A into master.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §17/§18">Every PR touching `.claude/` MUST add an entry to `.claude/CHANGELOG.md`. Update the root §17 Compose pointer row if the amendment changes what it says.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Owner sign-off on the residual list is REQUIRED (spec §Unresolved Questions names this as blocking FR-A10 and success criterion 5). An unsigned list does not complete this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT create a new architecture document that duplicates `COMPOSE-READ-REFERENCE-FIDELITY.md` — the write-side companion complements it (root §11).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ADR amendment, architecture documentation, residual loss</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file>.claude/CHANGELOG.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/COMPOSE-READ-REFERENCE-FIDELITY.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/adr-049-third-amendment-draft.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL; confirm MAIN SESSION execution; load the amendment draft, gate-decision.md, spec.md.</step>
    <step order="1">Apply the third amendment to `.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md` — concise + full forms, seven invariants, paired-MUST rule, invariant (7) as a general rule.</step>
    <step order="2">Compile the residual loss list from the final gate results: every construct family the gate does NOT preserve, with what specifically is lost.</step>
    <step order="3">Run the parity check: for each construct family, confirm gate-preserves XOR on-the-list. Record the check, including any family that fails parity (which is a defect, not a documentation choice).</step>
    <step order="4">Publish the list in `docs/architecture/` as the write-side companion to `COMPOSE-READ-REFERENCE-FIDELITY.md`.</step>
    <step order="5">Obtain owner sign-off and record it (who, when, on which version of the list).</step>
    <step order="6">Add the `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` entry; update the root §17 Compose pointer row if needed.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the parity check fails — a construct degrades that is not on the list, or the list names something the gate preserves — that is a defect in Track A or in the list. Fix it; do not publish a list you know does not match.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the owner declines to sign off on a residual item, that item becomes a scope question (fix it, or gate it via task 043) — not a documentation revision.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="adr">.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</output>
    <output type="doc">docs/architecture/ (write-side residual loss list)</output>
    <output type="doc">.claude/CHANGELOG.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>ADR-049 carries the third amendment in both concise and full forms.</criterion>
    <criterion>All seven invariants are stated, with (1) and (2) declared as a pair no future amendment may trade away singly.</criterion>
    <criterion>Invariant (7) is stated as a general rule, not per-surface.</criterion>
    <criterion>The residual loss list is published in `docs/architecture/` and names what is lost per construct family.</criterion>
    <criterion>A parity check is RECORDED demonstrating gate-preserves XOR on-the-list for every construct family.</criterion>
    <criterion>Owner sign-off is recorded with who, when, and which version of the list.</criterion>
    <criterion>`.claude/CHANGELOG.md` has an entry; the root §17 Compose pointer is current.</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: the amendment does not weaken or remove either of the paired MUSTs.</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: no new architecture document duplicates `COMPOSE-READ-REFERENCE-FIDELITY.md`.</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: the `.claude/` edits were applied by the MAIN SESSION, not delegated to a sub-agent.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
